message: "If you use this analysis or its figures, please cite it as below."
title: "Where AI Is Actually Used Across the Wage Distribution"
authors:
  - family-names: Daly
    given-names: Brendan
type: software
date-released: 2026-07-01
version: "1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/brdaly/ai-wages"
abstract: >-
  A short, reproducible empirical note joining the Anthropic Economic Index
  (observed AI use by occupation) to BLS occupational wages, and contrasting it
  with a legacy predicted-automatability index. Observed AI exposure rises with
  wages; predicted automatability falls with wages.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - labor economics
  - wages
  - AI adoption
  - Anthropic Economic Index
